_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 3
---
order: 3
---
short_label: V.3
---
statement: If a first magnitude is the same multiple of a second that a third is of a fourth, and if equimultiples are taken of the first and third, then the magnitudes taken also are equimultiples respectively, the one of the second and the other of the fourth.
---
proof:

Let a first magnitude *A* be the same multiple of a second *B* that a third *C* is of a fourth *D,* and let equimultiples *EF* and *GH* be taken of *A* and *C.*

I say that *EF* is the same multiple of *B* that *GH* is of *D.* [!just V.Def.2]

<figure class="diagram rdiagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="300" height="150" tabindex="0"></canvas>
